          MaskType      "SPI unpack"
          MaskDescription "This block unpacks float data sent over SPI. \n"
"\n"
"It first merges the recieved 16 bits words (uint16) two-by-two into uint32 (3"
"2 bits).\n"
"It interprets the array of unsigned integers (32 bits) as an array of floats "
"(32 bits).\n"
"\n"
"The SPI block must be configured to 16 bits per word and the number of words "
"per transmission is double the number of floats to be sent."
